'''Tatiana Andrea Calmell del Solar Ortega'''<ref>{{cite web |last=Palacios Yábar |first=Mijail |title=Tatiana Calmell: "El carisma es algo que nace contigo" |url=https://peru21.pe/cultura/tatiana-calmell-el-carisma-es-algo-que-nace-contigo/ |website=Perú21 |date=2024-04-13 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref> (born 22 July 1994) is a [[Peruvian]] model, actress, and beauty pageant titleholder who was crowned [[Miss Peru|Miss Peru 2024]]. She represented Peru at [[Miss Universe 2024]], reaching the Top 12 and receiving the title of Miss Universe Americas.

She previously placed as first runner-up at Miss Peru 2022 and represented Peru at [[Miss International 2022]], finishing as second runner-up.

== Early life and education==
Tatiana Andrea Calmell del Solar Ortega was born on 22 July 1994 in [[Breña]], [[Peru]] and raised in [[San Miguel District, Lima|San Miguel]]. Her father was an aeronautics specialist and former pilot for a major North American airline.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Tatiana Calmell del Solar: Todo sobre la flamante Miss Perú 2024|url=https://cosas.pe/belleza/309940/tatiana-calmell-del-solar-todo-sobre-la-flamante-miss-peru-2024/|website=Cosas|access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref> From a young age, she was involved in modeling, television commercials, and beauty pageants.<ref>{{cite web |last=Farroñay |first=Marylin |date=2024-06-10 |title=La biografía completa de Tatiana Calmell, Miss Perú 2024: edad, trayectoria profesional y vida sentimental |url=https://www.infobae.com/peru/2024/06/10/biografia-de-tatiana-calmell-miss-peru-2024-que-carrera-estudio-trayectoria-profesional-y-vida-sentimental/ |access-date=2024-09-06 |website=Infobae |language=es-ES}}</ref> She began studying [[Business Administration]] at the [[University of Piura]] but later shifted to [[fashion design]], after which she returned to professional modeling.

== Career ==
=== Modeling ===
At 14, Calmell launched her modeling career by participating in the Elite Model Look competition, where she competed with fellow Peruvian models such as [[Janick Maceta]] and Alondra García Miró.<ref>{{cite web |last=Retamal |first=Brenda García |date=2024-06-10 |title=Tatiana Calmell es coronada como Miss Perú 2024 en una ceremonia llena de emoción [VIDEO] - RPP Noticias |url=https://rpp.pe/cultura/mas-cultura/final-miss-peru-2024-en-vivo-hoy-tatiana-calmell-se-corona-como-la-ganadora-certamen-de-belleza-noticia-1560473 |access-date=2024-09-06 |website=RPP.pe |language=es}}</ref>

In 2013, she participated in the reality television show ''[[Peru's Next Top Model]]''. During the competition, she reported experiencing inappropriate conduct, which affected her performance and led to her elimination.<ref>{{cite web |last=República |first=La |date=2022-09-30 |title=La vez que Tatiana Calmell fue eliminada de un concurso en ATV por insinuar acoso sexual |url=https://larepublica.pe/espectaculos/2022/09/29/tatiana-calmell-del-solar-el-dia-que-la-actriz-fue-eliminada-de-perus-next-top-model-por-insinuar-acoso-de-antonio-borges |access-date=2024-09-06 |website=LaRepública.pe |language=es}}</ref>

=== Television and film ===
Calmell made her acting debut in 2020 in the telenovela ''[[Princesas (TV series)Princesas]]'',<ref>{{cite web |last=RPP Noticias |title="Princesas": ¿Qué dijeron las protagonistas de la telenovela sobre su primer día de estreno? |url=https://rpp.pe/tv/peru/princesas-que-dijeron-las-protagonistas-de-la-telenovela-sobre-su-primer-dia-de-estreno-noticia-1307899 |website=RPP Noticias |date=2020-12-02 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref> later reprising her role in the second season, renamed ''Brujas''.<ref>{{cite web |last=Ojo |title=Tatiana Calmell confirma que protagonizará 'Brujas', segunda parte de la telenovela 'Princesas' |url=https://ojo.pe/videos/ojo-show/tatiana-calmell-confirma-que-protagonizara-brujas-web-ojo-farandula-noticia/ |website=Ojo |date=2022-06-18 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref> Following her participation in [[Miss International 2022]], Calmell made her film debut in 2024 with ''Bienvenidos al paraíso''.<ref>{{cite web |last=RPP Noticias |title='Bienvenidos al paraíso' llega al streaming: la primera película peruana en Disney+ |url=https://rpp.pe/tv/streaming/bienvenidos-al-paraiso-llega-al-streaming-la-primera-pelicula-peruana-en-disney-noticia-1572089 |website=RPP Noticias |date=2024-08-28 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

== Pageantry ==
=== Miss Peru 2022 ===
Calmell competed in Miss Peru 2022, finishing as first runner-up, which qualified her to represent Peru at [[Miss International 2022]] in Tokyo.<ref>{{cite web |last=Miss International |title=Miss International 2022 Contestants |url=https://www.miss-international.org/en/2022/contestants/ |website=Miss International |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

=== Miss International 2022 ===
At [[Miss International 2022]], Calmell placed as second runner-up, marking Peru’s return to the semifinals after more than 50 years.<ref>{{cite web |last=El Comercio |first=Redacción EC |title=Miss International 2022: la peruana Tatiana Calmell obtuvo el tercer puesto del certamen |url=https://elcomercio.pe/luces/moda/miss-international-2022-la-peruana-tatiana-calmell-obtuvo-el-tercer-puesto-del-certamen-noticia/ |website=El Comercio |date=2022-12-13 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

She crowned her successor Camila Díaz in 2023 as Miss International Peru.<ref>{{cite web |title=Miss International 2023 Contestants |url=https://www.miss-international.org/en/2023/contestants/ |website=Miss International |access-date=2025-05-08}}</ref> At the time, Calmell believed her pageant career had ended due to age eligibility rules. However, during the same event, the [[Miss Universe Organization]] officially announced the elimination of its age limit, prompting her to return to competition.<ref>{{cite web |last=Bracamonte |first=Earl D.C. |title=Miss Universe scraps age limit, women of all ages can now join |url=https://www.philstar.com/lifestyle/fashion-and-beauty/2023/09/13/2295977/miss-universe-scraps-age-limit-women-all-ages-can-now-join |website=Philstar.com |date=2023-09-13 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

=== Miss Peru 2024 ===
Calmell competed again for Miss Peru in 2024, representing the province of [[Talara]]. She won the national title among 34 contestants <ref>{{Cite web|title=Miss Universe Contestants 2024|url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion-beauty/2024/06/17/miss-universe-contestants-2024/|website=The National|access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref> and was crowned by her predecessor, [[Camila Escribens]], at the end of the event.

=== Miss Universe 2024 ===
Representing Peru at [[Miss Universe 2024]] in [[Mexico City]], Calmell reached the Top 12 and earned the title of Miss Universe Americas, becoming the first Peruvian to achieve this recognition.<ref>{{cite web |last=Agencia Peruana de Noticias Andina |title=Miss Universo 2024: Miss Perú, Tatiana Calmell del Solar, quedó en el top 12 |url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-exportacion-prendas-terminadas-alpaca-se-incrementa-un-5-687689.aspx/noticia-miss-universo-2024-miss-peru-tatiana-calmell-del-solar-quedo-el-top-12-1008151.aspx |website=Agencia Peruana de Noticias Andina |date=2024-11-16 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

== Advocacy and platforms ==
Calmell has been involved in various social initiatives and advocacy efforts throughout her career. She participated in campaigns such as ''Dulces que Cumplen Deseos'', organized by the confectionery company [[La Ibérica]] in collaboration with Make-A-Wish Peru.

As Miss International Peru 2022, she served as an ambassador for organizations including the Peruvian League to Fight Cancer, Beauties for SDGs, and Corazones Verdes Mundial, supporting outreach efforts across different regions of the country. She took part in the International Forum of Women Entrepreneurs in Japan and developed a project at the Colegio Divino Niño Jesús, an institution offering specialized education and rehabilitation services for children. Motivated by the school's limited resources, she initiated efforts to support its educational programs and encouraged public involvement.<ref>{{cite web |last=El Especial |title=Miss Perú 2024: Tatiana Calmell [¡Entrevista Exclusiva!] |url=https://elespecial.com/miss-peru-2024-tatiana-calmell-entresvista-exclusiva |website=El Especial |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

Following her reign, she continued to collaborate with social organizations, becoming an ambassador for the [[Ronald McDonald House Charities]] and the [[Ministry of the Environment of Japan]]. She launched environmental initiatives such as "''Menos Plástico, Más Vida''" (Less Plastic, More Life) in partnership with these organizations and the María Reina de la Esperanza School, with which she has maintained long-term involvement.<ref>{{cite web |last=TVPerú |title=Ministerio del Ambiente promueve campaña 'Menos plástico, más vida' |url=https://tvperu.gob.pe/noticias/nacionales/ministerio-del-ambiente-promueve-campana-menos-plastico-mas-vida |website=TVPerú |date=2024-04-22 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

As Miss Peru 2024, Calmell has expressed a commitment to continuing work on social projects, particularly those focused on education and the empowerment of young women in rural communities.<ref>{{cite web |last=Vilela Monzón |first=Nilo |title=Miss Perú Universo llega a Chulucanas a ofrecer chocolatada solidaria |url=https://diariocorreo.pe/edicion/piura/miss-peru-universo-llega-chulucanas-ofrecer-chocolatada-solidaria-noticia/ |website=Diario Correo |date=2024-12-23 |access-date=2025-05-05}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
She has been in a long-term relationship with Peruvian [[surfer]] Cristóbal de Col.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Tatiana Calmell del Solar y Cristóbal de Col: La Reina y el Campeón|url=https://cosas.pe/personalidades/313079/tatiana-calmell-del-solar-y-cristobal-de-col-la-reina-y-el-campeon/|website=Cosas|access-date=31 May 2025}}</ref>

