'''Mariah Danae Antetokounmpo''' (née '''Riddlesprigger'''; born September 17, 1992) is an American entrepreneur and former [[volleyball]] player. She is married to [[National Basketball Association|NBA]] All-Star [[Giannis Antetokounmpo]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Saldajeno |first=Ivan |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo's wife Mariah Riddlesprigger shares new family holiday tradition on Instagram |work=Sportskeeda}}</ref>

== Early life and education ==
Born Mariah Danae Riddlesprigger in [[Fresno, California|Fresno]], California. She attended [[Rice University]] in Houston, Texas, where she earned a degree in Sports Management and Sociology in 2014. During her time at Rice, she played volleyball as an outside hitter for the university's team.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Who Is Giannis Antetokounmpo's Fiancée? All About Mariah Riddlesprigger |url=https://people.com/sports/who-is-mariah-riddlesprigger-giannis-antetokounmpo/ |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=People Magazine |language=en}}</ref>

== Career ==
Following her graduation from Rice University, Antetokounmpo interned with the [[NBA Summer League]] for two consecutive years. She later worked in the basketball operations department for the [[Philadelphia 76ers]].<ref name=":0" />

In 2021, Antetokounmpo launched her own apparel brand, "Sincerely, Mariah." The brand features loungewear with messages intended to promote positivity and self-empowerment. The creation of the brand was influenced by her experiences during the COVID-19 pandemic.<ref name=":0" />

Antetokounmpo is heavily involved in the Charles Antetokounmpo Family Foundation's (CAFF) impact and philanthropic work.{{Citation needed|date=April 2025}}

== Personal life ==
Mariah Antetokounmpo and [[Giannis Antetokounmpo]] were married on September 1, 2024, following a three-day celebration at the Costa Navarino resort near [[Pylos|Pylos, Greece]]. The wedding was attended by numerous high-profile guests, including [[LeBron James]], [[Jrue Holiday]], [[Serena Williams]], and Greek Prime Minister [[Kyriakos Mitsotakis]]. The couple's longtime friend and Bucks teammate [[Khris Middleton]] served as the best man.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-09-01 |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo and Mariah Riddlesprigger tied the knot with Khris Middleton being the best man |url=https://www.eurohoops.net/en/nba-news/1711542/giannis-antetokounmpo-and-mariah-riddlesprigger-tied-the-knot-with-khris-middleton-being-the-best-man/ |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=Eurohoops |language=en}}</ref>

The couple have been together since 2014, when they first met at the [[2014 NBA Summer League]].<ref>Giannis: The Marvelous Journey (film)</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=La Roche |first=Mariana |title=Giannis and Mariah engaged, announce they're expecting a baby girl |url=https://www.msn.com/en-us/music/news/giannis-and-mariah-engaged-announce-theyre-expecting-a-baby-girl/ar-AA1gzCXh?apiversion=v2&noservercache=1&domshim=1&renderwebcomponents=1&wcseo=1&batchservertelemetry=1&noservertelemetry=1 |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=MSN}}</ref> They have four children: Liam Charles (born 2020), Maverick Shai (born 2021), Eva Brooke (born 2023),<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-08-30 |title=Here's what we know and don't know about the reported Giannis Antetokounmpo and Mariah Riddlesprigger wedding this weekend in Greece |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/heres-know-dont-know-reported-165029103.html |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=Yahoo Sports |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo's 3 Kids: All About Liam, Maverick and Eva |url=https://people.com/parents/all-about-giannis-antetokounmpo-kids/ |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=Peoplemag |language=en}}</ref> and  Aria Capri (born 2025).<ref>{{cite web |last1=VanDerveer |first1=Melanie |title=Giannis And Mariah Antetokounmpo Adding A 4th To The Roster!|url=https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/giannis-mariah-antetokounmpo-adding-4th-231519891.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAESQFC9Usc6xfOrLQ15-P4qzfcaShnGe9PZM6P5Fo-aux-3wbx29QZfNzp8n06X7DnSrQQo3pU1tvjFEmkBHN6EXPWCRcfxEesXZZTYEoGVzQHt-JXEoiala_9thjJmlJr_QHuWKa0k54qrRDsi-j6gZb8a65mpCINwdUPCe2_bD |website=yahoo |access-date=February 22, 2024 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Grant |first1=Kayla |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo Welcomes Baby No. 4 with Wife Mariah and Shares the First Photo of His Baby Girl|url=https://people.com/giannis-antetokounmpo-welcomes-baby-no-4-with-his-wife-mariah-11727070 |website=people |access-date=May 1, 2025}}</ref> The family participates in various philanthropic activities, particularly in the [[Milwaukee]] area.<ref name=":2">{{Cite magazine |date=2024-08-30 |title=Bucks' Antetokounmpo reportedly to wed longtime partner Mariah Riddlesprigger this weekend in Greece |url=https://www.si.com/nba/bucks/news/millwaukee-bucks-star-giannis-antetokounmpo-longtime-partner-mariah-riddlesprigger-wedding-weekend-in-greece |access-date=2024-09-01 |magazine=Sports Illustrated |language=en-US}}</ref>  Mariah is [[Catholic Church|Catholic]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chrysopoulos |first=Philip |date=2024-09-01 |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo Wedding Went as Lavishly as Planned |url=https://greekreporter.com/2024/09/01/giannis-antetokounmpo-wedding-costa-navarino-greece-messenia-greek-freak/ |access-date=2025-07-08 |website=[[Greek Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

The Antetokounmpo family founded the Charles Antetokounmpo Family Foundation in 2022. The Foundation's work focuses their impact on supporting basic needs and leveraging the power of sport, and works across the three geographies the Antetokounmpos have called home: Greece, Nigeria, and Milwaukee, WI, USA.<ref name=":0" /><ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Giannis Antetokounmpo's Fiancée Mariah on Finding Her 'Own Identity' by 'Giving Back' to Milwaukee (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/giannis-antetokounmpo-fiancee-mariah-finds-passion-in-community-outreach-exclusive-8411566 |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=People Magazine |language=en}}</ref>

=== Advocacy and community involvement ===
Riddlesprigger is involved in advocacy for maternal and infant health, with a particular focus on addressing [[Race and health|racial disparities in healthcare]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Exclusive: Giannis and Mariah on getting engaged, their growing family, and the BIG reason they're helping other families |url=https://www.cbs58.com/news/Exclusive-Giannis-and-Mariah-on-getting-engaged-their-growing-family-and-the-BIG-reason-theyre-helping-other-families |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=CBS58 |language=en}}</ref> She has spoken about her own experiences with [[pre-eclampsia]] during her first pregnancy, which has informed her work in this area.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Jones |first=Bria |date=2024-05-11 |title=Black Birth Symposium brings attention to racial disparities |url=https://www.fox6now.com/news/black-birth-symposium-milwaukee-2024 |access-date=2024-09-01 |website=FOX6 News Milwaukee |language=en-US}}</ref> She is also a board member of the Milwaukee Diaper Mission.<ref name=":1" />

