'''Rebecca Kassay''' is an American politician who has served in the [[New York State Assembly]] representing the [[New York's 4th State Assembly district|4th District]] since 2025. A [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democrat]], she represents part of [[Suffolk County, New York|Suffolk County]].

== Early life ==
Rebecca Kassay was born in [[Stony Brook, New York]]. She was raised in [[St. James, New York|St. James]].<ref name="bio1"/> Kassay earned a bachelor's degree from the [[State University of New York at New Paltz]] in 2010.<ref name="bio1">{{cite web |title=Rebecca Kassay - Assembly District 4 {{!}}Assembly Member Directory {{!}} New York State Assembly |url=https://assembly.state.ny.us/mem/Rebecca-Kassay/bio/ |website=State Assembly |access-date=17 February 2026}}</ref>

== Political career ==
Kassay previously served as deputy mayor of [[Port Jefferson, New York|Port Jefferson]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Staff |first=T. B. R. |date=2024-04-12 |title=Port Jefferson Deputy Mayor Rebecca Kassay runs for NYS Assembly {{!}} TBR News Media |url=https://tbrnewsmedia.com/port-jefferson-deputy-mayor-rebecca-kassay-announces-run-for-nys-assembly/ |access-date=2024-11-13 |language=en-US}}</ref> She was elected a Village trustee in Port Jefferson in 2020.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Release |first=Press |date=2023-11-15 |title=Rebecca Kassay announces candidacy for New York State Assembly {{!}} TBR News Media |url=https://tbrnewsmedia.com/rebecca-kassay-announces-candidacy-for-new-york-state-assembly/ |access-date=2024-11-13 |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== New York State Assembly ===
In the [[2024 New York State Assembly election]], she unseated Republican [[Ed Flood]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bolger |first=Timothy |date=2024-11-11 |title=Long Island State Assembly Races See Two Upsets, Third Likely |url=https://www.longislandpress.com/2024/11/11/long-island-state-assembly-races-see-two-upsets-third-likely/ |access-date=2024-11-13 |website=www.longislandpress.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

