'''Hotaru Tsukamoto''' ({{langx|ja|塚本 蛍}}, Tsukamoto Hotaru; born 17 October 1999) is a Japanese softball player who plays as an outfielder for Honda Reverta and the Japan women's national softball team. She has won gold medals at the [[2022 Asian Games]], the [[2024 Women's Softball World Cup]] and the [[2026 Asian Games]].<ref name="JOC">{{cite web |title=塚本 蛍｜アスリート |trans-title=Hotaru Tsukamoto – Athlete profile |url=https://www.joc.or.jp/athletes/tsukamotohotaru/index.html |publisher=Japanese Olympic Committee |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref><ref name="Honda">{{cite web |title=選手・スタッフ紹介 |trans-title=Players and staff |url=https://www.honda-tochigi.com/softball/profile.html |publisher=Honda Reverta |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref>

== Career ==

Tsukamoto attended Saga Joshi Junior College High School in Saga Prefecture and subsequently joined Honda's women's softball team. She plays as an outfielder and has represented Honda in Japan's domestic softball competitions. She was named captain of Honda's team for the 2024 season.<ref name="JOC"/><ref name="Honda2024">{{cite web |title=2024年 選手・スタッフ紹介アーカイブ |trans-title=2024 player and staff profiles |url=https://www.honda-tochigi.com/softball/profile_2024.html |publisher=Honda Reverta |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref>

Tsukamoto became a member of Japan's senior women's national softball team and competed at the [[2022 Asian Games]] in Hangzhou, China, held in 2023. Japan won the women's softball tournament, earning the gold medal after defeating China in the final.<ref name="JOC"/>

In July 2024, Tsukamoto represented Japan at the [[2024 Women's Softball World Cup]] final stage in Castions di Strada, Italy. Japan defeated the United States 6–1 in the final to win the world title. Tsukamoto recorded a double during the championship game and contributed to Japan's victory.<ref name="WorldCup">{{cite web |title=女子TOP日本代表レポート |trans-title=Japan women's national team report |url=https://softball.or.jp/news/woman-2024/report/0720.html |publisher=Japan Softball Association |date=20 July 2024 |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref><ref name="WorldCupRoster">{{cite web |title=第17回女子ワールドカップ ファイナル 大会概要・出場選手 |trans-title=17th Women's Softball World Cup final: Tournament overview and roster |url=https://www.softball.or.jp/worldcup2024/ |publisher=Japan Softball Association |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref>

Tsukamoto was selected for Japan's team at the [[2026 Asian Games]] in Aichi and Nagoya. She appeared as an outfielder in the women's tournament, helping Japan progress through the preliminary round. In the game against Hong Kong on 28 September, she recorded a hit during Japan's 15–0 victory. She also hit a triple in the match against Singapore on 30 September, which Japan won 10–0.<ref name="AsianGamesRoster">{{cite web |title=第20回アジア競技大会 大会概要・出場選手 |trans-title=20th Asian Games: Tournament overview and roster |url=https://www.softball.or.jp/asian-games2026/ |publisher=Japan Softball Association |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=第20回アジア競技大会 試合レポート：予選ラウンド第２戦 日本 vs ホンコン・チャイナ |trans-title=20th Asian Games match report: Japan vs Hong Kong, China |url=https://www.softball.or.jp/asian-games2026/report/asian-games2026_game2.html |publisher=Japan Softball Association |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=第20回アジア競技大会 試合レポート：予選ラウンド第４戦 日本 vs シンガポール |trans-title=20th Asian Games match report: Japan vs Singapore |url=https://www.softball.or.jp/asian-games2026/report/asian-games2026_game4.html |publisher=Japan Softball Association |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref>

Japan finished the preliminary round undefeated and faced China in the gold-medal game on 3 October 2026. Tsukamoto started as the designated player in the final, in which Japan won 7–0 in five innings. The victory secured Japan's seventh consecutive Asian Games gold medal in women's softball, and Tsukamoto won her second Asian Games gold medal.<ref name="AsianFinal">{{cite web |title=第20回アジア競技大会 試合レポート：優勝決定戦 日本 vs 中国 |trans-title=20th Asian Games final: Japan vs China |url=https://www.softball.or.jp/asian-games2026/report/asian-games2026_final.html |publisher=Japan Softball Association |access-date=11 October 2026 |language=ja}}</ref><ref name="JOC"/>

